module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.EpiMono
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorDualSheafHom

/-!
# A monomorphism out of a rank-one module is a regular section of the sheaf-hom

Let `(C, J, 𝒪)` be a ringed site and let `E`, `F` be sheaves of `𝒪`-modules.  A morphism
`φ : E ⟶ F` is the same thing as a global section of the sheaf-hom `SheafHom(E, F)` of
[Stacks, Tag 03EM].  This file proves that if `φ` is a **monomorphism** and `E` is locally free
of rank one, then that global section is **regular** in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 01WY]:
multiplication by it is a monomorphism `𝒪 ⟶ SheafHom(E, F)`.

This is the half of the tensor–hom adjunction `Hom(𝒪, SheafHom(E, F)) ≅ Hom(E, F)` of
[Stacks, Tag 03EO] that *moves monomorphisms*.  The adjunction identifies the two hom-sets, but
a bijection of hom-sets does not by itself carry monicity of `φ` to monicity of the morphism
`𝒪 ⟶ SheafHom(E, F)` attached to it: the two are cancellation properties against different
test objects.  What makes the transport true is that `E` is locally generated by a single
section, so a local scalar that annihilates `φ` annihilates a local generator of `E`, hence
vanishes.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.homSections`: a morphism `E ⟶ F` of sheaves of modules, read as a
  global section of `SheafHom(E, F)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_unitHomEquiv_symm_homSections`: **a monomorphism `E ⟶ F` is a
  regular global section of `SheafHom(E, F)`**, provided `E` carries rank-one dual bases on a
  family of objects covering the final object.

## Implementation notes

The proof is sectionwise.  Monicity in `SheafOfModules` is reflected by the faithful forgetful
functor to presheaves of modules, so it is enough that multiplication by the global section is
injective on the sections over every object.  Two scalars `r`, `t` over `U` with
`r · (homSections φ) = t · (homSections φ)` restrict, along any `p : Z ⟶ U`, to scalars with
`r|_Z · φ(x) = t|_Z · φ(x)` for every section `x` of `E` over `Z`; since `φ` is injective on
sections this reads `r|_Z · x = t|_Z · x`.  Taking `Z` inside a member of the covering family
and `x` the rank-one generator of `E` there, the dual coordinate of the generator turns that
into `r|_Z = t|_Z`, and the structure sheaf is separated.

Everything is phrased through the pinned-down operations of
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/SheafHom.lean` — `dualEval`, `dualApp` and
`sheafHomEval` — rather than through `evalSection` directly.  The reason is the one given there:
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf` is not reducible, so the `ModuleCat`
index of a module over it and the index `Oforget 𝒪` that the internal hom carries, although
equal, are not connected by instance search, and a scalar multiplication written in the wrong
one of the two spellings fails to elaborate.

No hypothesis is placed on `F`, and `E` enters only through the rank-one dual bases — which is
also exactly the hypothesis under which `SheafHom(E, F)` is identified with `F ⊗ E^∨`
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_tensorDualToSheafHom`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03EM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03EM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03EO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03EO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite

universe v u w

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

/-! ### Multiplication by a global section, on the sections over an object -/

section Unit

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{w}}

/-- **Multiplication by a global section, read on the sections over an object of the site**: the
morphism `𝒪 ⟶ M` attached to a global section `m` of `M` sends a section `r` of the structure
sheaf to `r · m`. -/
theorem unitHomEquiv_symm_val_app_apply (M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{w} R) (m : M.sections)
    (U : Cᵒᵖ) (r : R.obj.obj U) :
    ((M.unitHomEquiv.symm m).val.app U).hom r = r • m.eval U := rfl

end Unit

/-! ### A morphism of sheaves of modules as a global section of the sheaf-hom -/

section Site

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  (𝒪 : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{max u v})
  (h𝒪 : Presheaf.IsSheaf J
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureRingPresheaf 𝒪))
  {E F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max u v}
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪)}

/-- **A morphism `E ⟶ F` of sheaves of modules, read as a global section of `SheafHom(E, F)`.**
A section of the sheaf-hom over `U` is a morphism `E|_U ⟶ F|_U` on the slice site at `U`
([Stacks, Tag 03EM]), and the global section is the family of all the restrictions of `φ`. -/
def homSections (φ : E ⟶ F) : (sheafHom 𝒪 h𝒪 E F).sections :=
  PresheafOfModules.sectionsMk (fun U => (restrFun 𝒪 U.unop).map φ.val)
    fun {_U _V} _f =>
      PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun _W => ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun _x => rfl)

@[simp]
theorem homSections_eval (φ : E ⟶ F) (U : Cᵒᵖ) :
    (homSections 𝒪 h𝒪 φ).eval U = (restrFun 𝒪 U.unop).map φ.val := rfl

/-- The global section attached to `φ` evaluates, on the sections over an object `U`, to `φ`
on the sections over `U`. -/
theorem sheafHomEval_homSections (φ : E ⟶ F) (U : C) (x : E.val.obj (op U)) :
    sheafHomEval 𝒪 h𝒪 ((homSections 𝒪 h𝒪 φ).eval (op U)) x =
      (φ.val.app (op U)).hom x := rfl

/-- The evaluation of a section of `SheafHom(E, F)` over `U` is linear in the section. -/
theorem sheafHomEval_smul {U : C}
    (r : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪).obj.obj (op U))
    (a : (sheafHom 𝒪 h𝒪 E F).val.obj (op U)) (x : E.val.obj (op U)) :
    sheafHomEval 𝒪 h𝒪 (r • a) x = r • sheafHomEval 𝒪 h𝒪 a x :=
  evalSection_smul_left 𝒪 E.val F.val (op U) r a x

/-- **The dual coordinate of a rank-one generator recovers the scalar.** -/
theorem dualEval_smul_e {U : C} (c : DualBasisOne 𝒪 h𝒪 E U)
    (a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪).obj.obj (op U)) :
    dualEval c.lam (a • c.e) = a := by
  rw [← dualApp_self, dualApp_smul, dualApp_self, c.eval_self]
  exact mul_one a

/-! ### Monicity transports to the global section -/

/-- **Two scalars multiplying a monomorphism to the same local morphism are equal**, when the
source of the monomorphism carries rank-one dual bases on a covering family.  This is the
sectionwise content of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_unitHomEquiv_symm_homSections`. -/
theorem eq_of_smul_homSections_eq {I : Type*} {Y : I → C} (hY : J.CoversTop Y)
    (b : ∀ i, DualBasisOne 𝒪 h𝒪 E (Y i)) (φ : E ⟶ F) (hφ : Mono φ) (U : Cᵒᵖ)
    (r t : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪).obj.obj U)
    (h : r • (homSections 𝒪 h𝒪 φ).eval U = t • (homSections 𝒪 h𝒪 φ).eval U) : r = t := by
  refine (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪)).isSheaf.isSeparated
      U.unop (Sieve.ofObjects Y U.unop) (hY U.unop) r t ?_
  rintro Z p ⟨i, ⟨q⟩⟩
  -- Restrict the hypothesis to `Z`.
  have hres : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪).obj.map p.op) r •
        (homSections 𝒪 h𝒪 φ).eval (op Z) =
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪).obj.map p.op) t •
        (homSections 𝒪 h𝒪 φ).eval (op Z) := by
    have h1 := congrArg (fun m => (sheafHom 𝒪 h𝒪 E F).val.map p.op m) h
    rw [PresheafOfModules.map_smul, PresheafOfModules.map_smul,
      PresheafOfModules.sections_property] at h1
    exact h1
  -- The two restricted scalars act in the same way on every section of `E` over `Z`.
  have hact : ∀ x : E.val.obj (op Z),
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪).obj.map p.op) r • x =
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪).obj.map p.op) t • x := by
    intro x
    have := hφ
    refine injective_val_app_of_mono φ (op Z) ?_
    have h2 := congrArg (fun a => sheafHomEval 𝒪 h𝒪 a x) hres
    rw [sheafHomEval_smul, sheafHomEval_smul, sheafHomEval_homSections] at h2
    exact ((φ.val.app (op Z)).hom.map_smul _ x).trans
      (h2.trans (((φ.val.app (op Z)).hom.map_smul _ x)).symm)
  -- On `Z` the module `E` has a rank-one generator, whose dual coordinate recovers the scalar.
  exact (dualEval_smul_e 𝒪 h𝒪 ((b i).restrict q) _).symm.trans
    ((congrArg (fun y => dualEval ((b i).restrict q).lam y) (hact ((b i).restrict q).e)).trans
      (dualEval_smul_e 𝒪 h𝒪 ((b i).restrict q) _))

/-- **A monomorphism `φ : E ⟶ F` is a regular global section of `SheafHom(E, F)`** when `E`
carries rank-one dual bases on a family of objects covering the final object: multiplication by
the global section `homSections φ` is a monomorphism `𝒪 ⟶ SheafHom(E, F)`.

This is [Stacks, Tag 01WY] regularity for the section of [Stacks, Tag 03EM] attached to `φ`,
and it is what carries monicity across the tensor–hom adjunction of [Stacks, Tag 03EO]. -/
theorem mono_unitHomEquiv_symm_homSections {I : Type*} {Y : I → C} (hY : J.CoversTop Y)
    (b : ∀ i, DualBasisOne 𝒪 h𝒪 E (Y i)) (φ : E ⟶ F) (hφ : Mono φ) :
    Mono ((sheafHom 𝒪 h𝒪 E F).unitHomEquiv.symm (homSections 𝒪 h𝒪 φ)) := by
  have hreflect : Functor.ReflectsMonomorphisms (_root_.SheafOfModules.forget.{max u v}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf 𝒪 h𝒪)) :=
    Functor.reflectsMonomorphisms_of_faithful _
  refine hreflect.reflects _ (PresheafOfModules.mono_of_injective fun U r t hrt => ?_)
  exact eq_of_smul_homSections_eq 𝒪 h𝒪 hY b φ hφ U r t
    ((unitHomEquiv_symm_val_app_apply (sheafHom 𝒪 h𝒪 E F) (homSections 𝒪 h𝒪 φ) U r).symm.trans
      (hrt.trans
        (unitHomEquiv_symm_val_app_apply (sheafHom 𝒪 h𝒪 E F) (homSections 𝒪 h𝒪 φ) U t)))

end Site

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
